{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "ae-clusters — one recording, three ways to read it (manual ch. 26-29).",
    "",
    "`family0..3` are one `multicluster` each: the same file, sliced at its onsets",
    "and sorted into four timbre families (darkest first). Every step all four",
    "draw the same random slice and only its family plays it — so each track is",
    "that family's mixer strip, with its own rate, pan and sends. `window` is a",
    "`slicer` on the same file: a looping window relocated by every step (full",
    "play area), its rate and loop end drawn by two `curveloop` shapes running at",
    "different speeds. `reader` is a `microsampler` whose micro-loops turn",
    "velocity into shape.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /family0                     the families and how many slices each got",
    "  /family3 gain=0              take one timbre out; /family3 rate=0.5 to pitch it",
    "  /family0 clusters=6          re-cluster (every instance should agree)",
    "  /window dev_slice=0 dev_rate=0   a plain looper; drag start/end",
    "  /rateshape rnd=now           draw a new rate curve",
    "  /reader vel_invert=on        loud hits become textures instead of tones",
    "  /family0 sample=random       a new recording for one family (the others keep theirs)"
  ],
